    "body": "## Problem\r\n\r\nThe `#has-parent?` predicate indexes the result of `node:parent()` without checking it, so a capture that matches a tree's root node raises\r\n\r\n    query.lua:600: attempt to index a nil value\r\n\r\ninstead of simply not matching. In a highlights query that breaks highlighting for the whole buffer. The sibling `#has-ancestor?` predicate handles the same situation.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nTreat a missing parent as \"does not match\".",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-06T16:27:03Z",
